misc: eeprom: Add optoe_i3c, native-I3C CMIS EEPROM driver

Add optoe_i3c, an I3C sibling of the optoe driver, for optical
transceivers that expose a native I3C management interface
(single-address, paged CMIS: QSFP-DD / OSFP).

The CMIS lower/upper page and bank state machine and the "eeprom" sysfs
ABI are kept from optoe. At the bus level, the I2C combined transfers
are replaced by I3C SDR private transfers issued through
i3c_device_do_priv_xfers(), and a transceiver is matched by the
Provisioned ID (PID) written to the driver's new_id attribute before
targets are enumerated. Legacy two-address SFP optics have no native
single-device I3C analogue and are not handled.

Matching IDs are not compiled in. new_id must be populated before the
I3C master runs DAA (dynamic address assignment): targets are bound as
they are enumerated, so IDs written afterwards will not match devices
that were already added. Write the manufacturer ID, optionally followed
by the part ID, to new_id before the master is registered:

  # manuf only: matches any part from that vendor
  echo 0x1abc > /sys/bus/i3c/drivers/optoe_i3c/new_id

  # manuf + part: matches that specific part only
  echo 0x1abc 0x5678 > /sys/bus/i3c/drivers/optoe_i3c/new_id

  # show the programmed IDs
  cat /sys/bus/i3c/drivers/optoe_i3c/new_id

The PID instance bits (15:12) are not compared. Once bound, the module
EEPROM is exposed at /sys/bus/i3c/devices/<bus>-<pid>/eeprom.

* Add drivers/misc/eeprom/optoe_i3c.c
* Add Kconfig entry EEPROM_OPTOE_I3C (depends on I3C && SYSFS)
* Build optoe_i3c from drivers/misc/eeprom/Makefile

Signed-off-by: Pavan Naregundi <pnaregundi@marvell.com>
--- a/drivers/misc/eeprom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/misc/eeprom/Kconfig
@@ -137,4 +137,23 @@ config EEPROM_OPTOE
 
 	  If unsure, say N.
 
+config EEPROM_OPTOE_I3C
+	tristate "read/write access to native-I3C SFP*/QSFP* EEPROMs"
+	depends on I3C && SYSFS
+	help
+	  If you say yes here you get support for read and write access to the
+	  EEPROM/register space of optical transceivers that present a native
+	  I3C management interface (single-address, paged CMIS/QSFP-DD/OSFP
+	  modules). This is the I3C sibling of the optoe (I2C) driver: devices
+	  are matched by Provisioned ID and the EEPROM is exported at
+	  /sys/bus/i3c/devices/<bus>-<pid>/eeprom.
+
+	  This driver only manages read/write access to the EEPROM, all other
+	  features should be accessed via the I3C bus directly.
+
+	  This driver can also be built as a module.  If so, the module
+	  will be called optoe_i3c.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
 endmenu
